# Everything uploaded here gets a public URL, so the bundle carries the site
# and its API and nothing else.
#
# schema.sql in particular published the table structure, the RLS policy logic
# and every settings key at /supabase/schema.sql — no credentials, but a map of
# exactly what to probe. The audit folder additionally served a fake admin
# login form from the real domain.

audit/
supabase/
tests/

*.md
BRAND_GUIDE.txt
design-qa.md

# Release archives are a product, not a page. Every zip under downloads/ was a
# public URL: 115 builds of a paid plugin, plus an unauthenticated update
# manifest that named the newest one. They now live in releases/ and reach
# customers through /api/download, which asks for a licence first.
releases/

# The source of both editions. WordPress is GPL and its source travelling with
# a customer is fine; serving the Universal tree from the marketing site is
# giving away the commercial edition. Neither is needed to render a page.
wordpress/
universal/

# Build and maintenance tooling. Runs here, never from a URL.
scripts/
